[13.59,"o","note: the region eu-south-2 does not offer c6a.xlarge, the template's default for MasterNodeInstanceType: using c5.xlarge (--aws-instance-type picks another)\r\nnote: the region eu-south-2 does not offer c6a.2xlarge, the template's default for MediaNodeInstanceType: using c5.2xlarge (--aws-instance-type picks another)\r\n"]
[14.276,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what ov does in your AWS account (region eu-south-2); --debug shows every command:\r\n\r\n  1. SSH key: import the stack's own key pair into the region (.openvidu/aws/openvidu-e2e-aws-ha-a102129-key.pem)\r\n  2. Template: render the high availability template into .openvidu/aws/cf-openvidu-pro-ha.yaml\r\n     and its parameters into .openvidu/aws/cfn-parameters.json (0600)\r\n  3. Bucket: stage the template in the S3 bucket openvidu-cfn-templates-***-eu-south-2 (created once, reused by every stack)\r\n  4. Network: the region's default VPC, vpc-0e2358cb016b9fef5, and its default subnets: subnet-0497cd2d92bbfd794 (eu-south-2a), subnet-02776aa519c2198f1 (eu-south-2b), subnet-0053e4f7269e42ebc (eu-south-2c)\r\n     the masters in subnet-0497cd2d92bbfd794 (eu-south-2a), subnet-02776aa519c2198f1 (eu-south-2b), subnet-0053e4f7269e42ebc (eu-south-2c); the media nodes in all of them\r\n     WARNING: three zones only, so eu-south-2a holds master-1 and master-4, and losing that zone\r\n     stops the stack (its state, MongoDB, Redis Sentinel and MinIO need three masters of the four).\r\n     A fourth zone avoids it: pass your own network with --param, four subnets in four zones.\r\n  5. Machines: Create the CloudFormation stack openvidu-e2e-aws-ha-a102129 with the four masters and the media nodes: master-1 installs OpenVidu and the rest join it (about 10 minutes)\r\n  6. Domain: openvidu-ha-test.dev.openvidu.io: the stack points it at the load balancer (an alias record) in the Route 53 zone ***, and deletes the record with the stack\r\n     openvidu-ha-test.dev.openvidu.io: the stack requests its ACM certificate, validated by DNS in that zone (a few minutes more)\r\n  7. Wait for OpenVidu to be up, read what it published (URL, credentials) and register this directory as the stack\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\r\n▶ Create the machines on AWS…\r\n   · SSH key pair for this stack: .openvidu/aws/openvidu-e2e-aws-ha-a102129-key.pem\r\n"]
[22.068,"o","   · import its public half into eu-south-2 as the key pair openvidu-e2e-aws-ha-a102129-key\r\n"]
[24.307,"o","   · create the CloudFormation stack openvidu-e2e-aws-ha-a102129 from .openvidu/aws/cf-openvidu-pro-ha.yaml (this returns when CloudFormation is done)\r\n"]
